Package: rrpplatform
Type: Package
Title: Internal Readmission Risk Pool Implementation
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(person("Alex", "Zajichek", email = "alexzajichek@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")), person("CentralStatz Statistical & Data Sciences LLC", role = "cph"))
Description: Establishes the main internal implementation package for the
    Readmission Risk Pool software and its one-way dependency on the focused
    runtime package. It opens validated installed-resource catalogs from an
    explicit software root, resolves declared resources by logical identity,
    compiles a supported six-path standard project-authoring convention plus
    bounded declarative branding resources into
    the unchanged raw producer and provider registration contracts,
    reports resource validation through a common privacy-safe result,
    normalizes installed canonical and five-resource runtime authority into
    exact runtime contexts, loads one explicit independent project through strict
    project-manifest and trusted-registration boundaries, executes its exact
    selected producer through a closed request/result boundary, delegates
    successful canonical admission to the runtime package, validates exact
    semantic provider declarations, executes the explicitly selected provider
    through the runtime package's closed risk boundary, transactionally
    initializes the smallest valid standard-authored project, and reports
    bounded operation results. It also realizes the supplied deterministic
    fictional project from cataloged templates without generating its source
    implicitly. It initializes, inspects, backs up, and restores explicit
    project-owned state and privately realizes the storage-neutral history port
    through bounded DBI and DuckDB sessions. It derives one deterministic,
    detached, conforming three-member logical product set from an explicitly
    selected complete governed history scope. It publishes one closed staged
    DCF/CSV product realization under project state and reopens validated,
    detached logical product access without exposing physical storage details.
    It also constructs and launches one installed, analytically read-only
    supplied Shiny application from a detached product snapshot and a bounded
    interpretation of standard project branding. It also provides a bounded
    read-only project lifecycle status, composes logical product construction
    with atomic materialization, prepares only the supplied fictional source,
    and validates the dependency-light software lifecycle authorities needed
    by later distribution work. It also supplies a thin version-specific
    command dispatcher with deterministic private-library and installed-resource
    preflight, explicit project lifecycle, durable run, focused history,
    product, and application intentions, controlled correction/restore
    confirmation, and privacy-safe human or JSON rendering.
